 \le L\zeta_1\|\widehat F-F\|_{\max}
   +L\|\widehat F\|_{\max}\|\widehat W-W\|_{2,\infty}.
 \tag{1}\] Here the last norm is the largest row Euclidean norm. Expand each summand as \((\widehat F-F)_{\mu\nu}W_{\nu,:}
+\widehat F_{\mu\nu}(\widehat W-W)_{\nu,:}\) and apply the triangle inequality to prove (1). Exactness follows if the subspace contains the row and column spaces of \(F\) and the column space of \(W\). This is a valid common-subspace bound, not a recovery of the original singular-tail-only bound.

